attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `ymgI`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 1% of calls {S1}. The model names 96% of them, at 0.32 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **Then 79 fork and variable columns run to the window's end**, carried by 40 to 89%, 64 persistent and 15 shell, in a region of plasticity in 1 to 89% of calls {S2}. A branch of 10 families runs through columns 1 to 10, a parallel path in 10 to 11% {S2.b1}. The `potA` to `potD` genes, columns 25 to 28, are [[spermidine/putrescine transport]] {S2.c25-28, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 90%, and hesitates less there, 0.32 against 0.50 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 3, `ymgF`, a fork column, 1.70 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in the `flgL` to `flgM` genes**, columns 67 to 79, [[flagellar basal body]] {S2.c67-79, Q}. The last column is `flgM`, in 40% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 90% of genes**, 0.50 bits on average, perplexity 1.6 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.25 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 76% against 97% {C}.

